  "body": "## What changed\n- 96 suite headers that still named a module M4.1 moved out of app as `app::<module>` now name the owner crate (`post::post`, `sim::verify`, `motion::machining2d`, `tools::*`, `cl::cl`, `geometry::geo2d`, ...). Header lines only: no test body changed, `#[test]` count unchanged.\n- `heidenhain_cycles` has a Gate map (`post::post (cnc, engine, probe_rec), cl::cl`).\n- xtask: `scan::app_reexports` reads `crates/app/src/lib.rs`'s `pub use camcraft_<crate>::...` re-exports; `quick::map_modules` also matches the legacy `app::<name>` spelling for the owner crate's module, so a stale header can never again hide its suite. Quick selects more, never less.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/922-gate-maps-moved-modules.md` (both rewrite and alias, why).\n\n## Selection, before / after (dry run, one probe line in each of `post/src/post/cnc.rs`, `sim/src/verify/mod.rs`, `motion/src/machining2d/mod.rs`)\n| change | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `sim::verify` | 28 suites | 60 suites |\n| `motion::machining2d` | 39 suites | 68 suites |\n| `post::post::cnc` (submodule narrowing: suites naming `cnc`) | 1 suite | 4 suites |\n\n## Pinning tests (xtask)\n- `a_post_module_change_selects_the_dialect_suites_by_new_and_old_map`\n- `a_sim_module_change_selects_the_suites_naming_verify`\n- `a_motion_module_change_selects_the_suites_naming_machining2d`\n- `app_reexports_lists_owner_crate_and_name`\n- `no_suite_names_a_moved_module_as_app_and_heidenhain_has_a_map` (walks the real tree)\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): xtask unit tests, 37 passed. The app suites were not run: only their `//!` headers changed.\n\n## Not exercised\nUi/app suites themselves (header comments only). #923 (a `.cps`/`.mch`-only diff selects nothing) is untouched and not made harder.\n\n## Process\n`xtask/` is a process file: `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 16 -> 17. A fork needs nothing beyond the normal process sync.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nFork synced at v0.17.0\n\nFixes #922\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
